doc='''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"><title>Greece, Bulgaria & North Macedonia — Artline museum research</title><style>'''+css+'''</style></head><body><div class="wrap"><header class="top"><span>Artline / Museum research<br>11 October 2026</span><nav><a href="#collections">Museum selections</a><a href="#research">Evidence & coverage</a></nav></header><main><section class="hero"><div><h1>Greece, Bulgaria<br>& North Macedonia</h1><p class="lead">Ancient sculpture, Byzantine icons and modern painting: 272 source-backed works across 22 museum collections.</p><p>185 authentic artwork images are prepared. Nineteen museums have an illustrated selection; three still need a verified photograph.</p><div class="status"><strong>Research prepared. Artline delivery pending.</strong><br>Google Cloud sign-in expired during upload. No artwork records have been added or changed by this pass. The report’s images are available locally.</div></div>'''+figure(hero,True)+'''</section><section class="scope"><div><h2>What this pass adds</h2><p>Greece includes Greek Macedonia. North Macedonia is treated separately. These are selected additions to the research, with documented museum connections and explicit unknown fields.</p><p>The existing Greek catalogue already contains 3,953 works across 80 institutions, including 2,023 artwork images. Those earlier holdings are listed separately in the coverage notes.</p><div class="downloads"><a href="selected-artworks.csv" download>Download artwork CSV</a><a href="museum-directory.csv" download>Download museum directory</a></div></div><table><thead><tr><th>Country</th><th>Museums</th><th>Works</th><th>Images</th></tr></thead><tbody>'''+rows+'''</tbody></table></section><section id="collections"><h2>Explore the museum selections</h2><p>Each illustrated museum opens with a photograph of an artwork. Expand an entry to see every selected work, its date and its source.</p><div class="tools"><label>Country<select id="country"><option value="">All countries</option><option value="GR">Greece</option><option value="BG">Bulgaria</option><option value="MK">North Macedonia</option></select></label><label class="search">Museum, city, artwork or artist<input id="search" type="search" placeholder="Try Ohrid, Piraeus or an artist’s name"></label><button id="reset" type="button">Reset</button><p id="results" role="status">22 museums</p></div><div id="empty" class="empty">No museum matches this search. Clear a filter to see more collections.</div>'''+''.join(sections)+'''</section><section id="research" class="research"><h2>Evidence, gaps & coverage</h2><p>The directory and object research are separate. An institution appearing in an official list does not establish a collection item or a matching photograph.</p><details open><summary>What was checked</summary><ul><li>710 directory entries: 214 from Greece’s Ministry of Culture directory, 477 Bulgarian registry entries including collection branches, and 19 from North Macedonia’s public-information directory. This is not a complete national census of museums.</li><li>The Greek directory work was carried forward from 8 October. All 80 existing Greek collection websites were checked again for this pass. In Bulgaria, 135 distinct registry website addresses were checked; failures and inaccessible pages remain recorded.</li><li>Object research used museum collection pages, inventory captions, museum APIs and illustrated catalogues. Selected Greek catalogue plates were inspected for the physical object, page caption, date and version.</li><li>Metadata is limited to works made by 1970, with unknown or conflicting dates held for editorial review. Museum-source images in this pass require evidence of creation by 1955.</li><li>Photographs retain their original composition, framing and margins. Source details and catalogue pages are labelled. Copyright labels and photography credits are preserved; inclusion does not imply an independently obtained licence.</li><li>Museum ownership is distinct from current display. Historic catalogue ownership is not a fresh on-view claim.</li></ul></details><details><summary>Unresolved objects and image gaps</summary><ul><li><strong>Kumanovo, Veles and Tetovo:</strong> five paintings have catalogue ownership evidence but no matching photograph in the inspected 2013 and 1984 publications. They remain useful metadata records without substituted images.</li><li><strong>Ahinora:</strong> the 1925 painting is documented at Kazanlak’s Ahinora Museum. Artline already has separate 1922 and 1925 records; the 1925 object needs a museum-link reconciliation rather than another artwork record. '''+link('https://www.artgallerykazanlak.com/en/exhibitions/ahinora/','Museum’s version history')+'''</li><li><strong>Lucifer, Lake Léman and Karlovo Courtyard:</strong> existing-record and version questions remain held. The existing Lucifer record cites an Art Institute of Chicago object, so it must not be assumed to be Sofia’s painting.</li><li><strong>National Gallery of North Macedonia:</strong> catalogue entries 13 and 35 contain conflicting translated dates. Entry 73 has conflicting ownership captions and is excluded.</li><li><strong>Skopje contemporary art:</strong> some caption years disagree with image filenames. Caption dates are preserved as evidence; these disagreements are recorded. A crossed-out placeholder and explicitly upscaled files were excluded.</li><li><strong>Pella:</strong> nine selected image downloads failed to connect. Eros and Psyche is verified and supplies the museum’s artwork photograph.</li><li><strong>Aigai:</strong> the requested catalogue returned an access-denied response. No attempt was made to bypass it and no objects were inferred from it.</li><li><strong>Loan exhibitions:</strong> private lenders, a Stobi find now in Belgrade, and temporary archaeological exhibits without clear collection ownership were excluded from museum assignments.</li></ul><p>Detailed review decisions are preserved in <a href="additional-review-notes.json">the review notes</a> and the source receipts beside this report.</p></details><details><summary>Existing Greek catalogue: 80 institutions</summary><p>Snapshot taken before this pass. These counts are existing Artline records, not additions claimed by this research. Seventy-four institutions already had at least one artwork image. Empty institutional research records are excluded from these catalogue counts.</p><div class="scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Museum or collection</th><th>City</th><th>Works</th><th>Images</th></tr></thead><tbody>'''+base_rows+'''</tbody></table></div></details><details id="directory"><summary>Search the 710-entry directory ledger</summary><p>Official directory entries include branches and specialised collections. Many still need object-level research. A link opens the directory evidence. Greek entries retain their original 8 October check date.</p><div class="directory-tools"><input id="directory-search" type="search" aria-label="Search museum directory" placeholder="Search directory name or city"><select id="directory-country" aria-label="Directory country"><option value="">All countries</option><option value="GR">Greece</option><option value="BG">Bulgaria</option><option value="MK">North Macedonia</option></select><span id="directory-count" role="status">710 entries</span></div><div class="scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Country</th><th>Institution or branch</th><th>City / region</th></tr></thead><tbody id="directory-rows">'''+dir_rows+'''</tbody></table></div></details><details><summary>Delivery status and preserved evidence</summary><p>138 image files reached private production storage before Google Cloud required reauthentication. No artwork records, museum links or image attachments were changed. All 185 reviewed image derivatives are available in this report.</p><p>The first selection has a recorded production duplicate review. The second and third selections still require a fresh live identity check before insertion. Selected new records will remain in review. Existing artwork metadata, images and creator links will be preserved.</p><p>The real local catalogue was not modified. Recovery backup, source originals, checksums, planned records and image review receipts are retained. Source originals are stored outside Documents.</p><div class="downloads"><a href="report-summary.json">Research counts</a><a href="report-artworks.json">Full artwork evidence</a><a href="delivery-access-hold.json">Upload interruption record</a></div></details></section></main></div><footer><div class="wrap"><p>Prepared for Artline. Sources checked 10–11 October 2026, except the explicitly identified earlier Greek directory research.</p><p>Titles and creator labels follow the cited sources. Unknown makers and disputed dates remain explicit.</p></div></footer><script>
const country=document.querySelector('#country'),search=document.querySelector('#search'),cards=[...document.querySelectorAll('.museum')];
function filter(){const q=search.value.trim().toLocaleLowerCase(),c=country.value;let n=0;for(const el of cards){const show=(!c||el.dataset.country===c)&&(!q||el.dataset.search.includes(q));el.hidden=!show;if(show)n++}document.querySelector('#results').textContent=n+' museum'+(n===1?'':'s');document.querySelector('#empty').style.display=n?'none':'block'}
country.addEventListener('change',filter);search.addEventListener('input',filter);document.querySelector('#reset').addEventListener('click',()=>{country.value='';search.value='';filter()});
const dr=[...document.querySelectorAll('#directory-rows tr')],ds=document.querySelector('#directory-search'),dc=document.querySelector('#directory-country');function directoryFilter(){const q=ds.value.toLocaleLowerCase().trim(),c=dc.value;let n=0;for(const el of dr){const show=(!c||el.dataset.country===c)&&(!q||el.dataset.search.includes(q));el.hidden=!show;if(show)n++}document.querySelector('#directory-count').textContent=n+' entries'}ds.addEventListener('input',directoryFilter);dc.addEventListener('change',directoryFilter);
</script></body></html>'''
